From 48ff2f770c00a72e086ed504c4430ebafa246da6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:24:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-57: fixes from a second review (R45-R49), and a
 placing bug the tests then found (0.57.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A second read-only review of HTDESIGNER-52..56; each point checked, fixed,
tested:
- WordWrap labels: BCB6 draws an AutoSize label that wraps with a fixed
  width and a height that follows the text; the generator writes exactly
  that (width px + height:auto). The probe read only width:auto, so it said
  AutoSize off (a false "AutoSize False / True" in the DFM list) and the
  reset wrote width:auto, letting the text wrap at the container's edge.
  Now a label is AutoSize when its width OR its height is auto, and turning
  AutoSize on for a label that wraps writes height:auto only.
- AutoSize off on a label that is not drawn (hidden, a tab not shown)
  measured 0 x 0 and wrote it; now refused with the reason (a size from the
  DFM still works).
- the spacing snap of a resize handle tested "same row" with sides the
  handle does not move (the mouse drifting down); now only the moving sides.
- DFM 位置 clicked twice while the first "on" still waited stayed on; a
  second click now counts as off.
- Tab order: the stops are read again after a selection change and after
  the eye (a tab switch no longer shows old numbers for a moment).
Found on the way by the new tests: putting a toolbox tool down on a point
where a resize handle of the selection sits looked up our own overlay, not
the page, so the component fell onto the form. The overlay is now out of the
way while looking.

Tests: probe (a wrap label reads on, on keeps the width, a hidden one is
refused; a right handle dragged with the mouse 76 px below still lands 8 px
before its neighbour; placing with the button selected finds its panel),
smoke (the ghost toggle clicked twice quickly ends off), real VS Code
(Setup.Contact lblWarning1 reads AutoSize on, as in its .dfm).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
